@startuml RuntimeArchitecture
!include ../themes/dark-theme.puml
title Central Auth Service - Runtime Architecture and Trust Boundaries

actor Client
cloud "TLS / optional mTLS boundary" as Transport
component "gRPC AuthService\nAuthGrpcService" as Grpc
package "Application" {
  component "Command handlers" as Handlers
  component "Domain services\nAuthentication / Token / TOTP" as Domain
  interface "Ports" as Ports
}
package "Infrastructure adapters" {
  component "JOOQ adapters\nusers, TOTP, refresh, revocation" as Jooq
  component "JWT signer / verifier" as Jwt
  component "Bucket4j limiters" as Bucket
  component "KeySupplier" as Keys
  component "gRPC TLS config" as Tls
}
database "PostgreSQL" as Db
folder "private_schema\nowner_role only" as Private
folder "api_schema\nSECURITY DEFINER functions" as Api

Client --> Transport
Transport --> Grpc
Grpc --> Handlers
Handlers --> Domain
Handlers --> Ports
Ports <.. Jooq
Ports <.. Jwt
Ports <.. Bucket
Jooq --> Api : EXECUTE only
Api --> Private : fixed search_path\ncontrolled results
Private --> Db
Api --> Db
Jwt --> Keys
Jooq --> Keys : TOTP encryption key
Transport --> Tls
Tls --> Keys : keystore passwords

note right of Transport
  Plaintext is possible only when no
  keystore path is configured. A truststore
  enables required client certificates.
end note
note bottom of Api
  PUBLIC execution is revoked; app role
  receives only required function grants.
end note

note bottom of Grpc
  AuthService currently has no access-token
  authentication interceptor or protected
  business RPC. verifyAccessToken is used by
  logout and is available for future consumers.
end note
@enduml